{"id": "npdenali", "name": "Denali National Park and Preserve", "short": "Denali", "place": "Alaska, USA", "lat": 63.33, "lon": -150.5, "side": "r", "cont": "North America", "country": "United States of America", "states": ["Alaska"], "kind": "Polar & mountain", "park": true, "blurb": "Caribou, wolves and grizzlies on tundra beneath North America's tallest peak.", "tip": {"id": "hare", "title": "Crash the hare cycle", "text": "Lynx lean on snowshoe hares, and foxes, eagles and wolves eat them too. Set Snowshoe hare to -100% and watch the lynx first, then the other predators."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Denali National Park and Preserve", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denali_National_Park_and_Preserve"}, {"title": "NPS: Mammals of Denali", "url": "https://www.nps.gov/dena/learn/nature/mammals.htm"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Arctic ground squirrel", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic_ground_squirrel"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Canada lynx", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canada_lynx"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Dall sheep", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dall_sheep"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Caribou", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caribou"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Denali National Park and Preserve", "icon": "ice", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "lichen", "sp": "cladonia rangiferina", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "A pale ground lichen of tundra and open spruce woods. Wikipedia calls it the favourite food of caribou, which dig through snow to reach it."}, {"id": "crowberry", "sp": "empetrum nigrum", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "bilberry", "sp": "vaccinium uliginosum", "xh": 0.5}, {"id": "willow", "sp": "salix", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "fireweed", "sp": "chamaenerion angustifolium", "xh": 0.9, "desc": "A 